cvc5 does not support more than 2 arguments to str.< (rejects the 3-arg :chainable form with a parse error and exits the process), which makes the exact number of subsequent IOException-tagged commands in the .err golden a non-deterministic OS-timing race rather than a stable value -- see err_stringLTSortMismatch.tst for a stable, non-racing proof that cvc5 rejects the construct at all.
